Laravel 12 and 13. Views in resources/views/errors/<status>.blade.php are used for abort(<status>) and framework errors (404, 500, 503 have Laravel defaults, so each needs its own file; 5xx.blade.php covers other 5xx such as 502, and 4xx.blade.php covers the other 4xx. Laravel ships bare default pages for 401, 402, 403, 404, 419 (expired form), 429 (throttled), 500 and 503, and those win over 4xx/5xx.blade.php, so copy 4xx.blade.php to 403.blade.php, 419.blade.php and 429.blade.php too). ModelNotFoundException becomes a 404 automatically. The bootstrap/app.php blocks of the headers, health-endpoint, robots-sitemap and error-pages recipes are parts of one ->withRouting/->withMiddleware/->withExceptions chain: merge them, each call once. Keep the layout free of DB queries, session and auth reads (an error page that throws is a second error), and set APP_DEBUG=false in production: with true, Laravel shows its debug page and leaks config instead of these views.
