Laravel 12 and 13. Mode comes from DEPLOY_ENV only ("production" is the only production value; unset = non-production). env() is read in config/app.php only, because env() returns null outside config files once `php artisan config:cache` ran; code reads config('app.deploy_env'). `config:cache` freezes DEPLOY_ENV at the moment it runs: run it on the host or image that has the right value, never copy a production cache into preview. Delete public/robots.txt (the skeleton ships one and the web server would serve it before this route). routes/stateless.php is shared with the health-endpoint recipe: keep both route sets in that one file. The bootstrap/app.php blocks of the headers, health-endpoint, robots-sitemap and error-pages recipes are parts of one ->withRouting/->withMiddleware/->withExceptions chain: merge them, each call once. Routes live outside the web group so no session cookie is sent. This sitemap is hand-rolled Blade (framework only); static files in public/ are served by the web server and do not get the X-Robots-Tag header, so set it in the non-production server config too.
